# Test vectors ported from Artio (https://github.com/real-logic/artio).
# Copyright 2015-2025 Real Logic Limited, Adaptive Financial Consulting Ltd. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
# Upstream has no NOTICE file. Messages are the constants in
# artio-codecs/src/test/java/uk/co/real_logic/artio/util/TestMessages.java (Java octal escapes
# evaluated; non-ASCII bytes replaced by '?' as String.getBytes(US_ASCII) does) and are cited by
# the test that uses them. '|' is SOH. expect=ok validate and non-zero frame vectors re-verified
# with python3.
#
# Not ported / deliberately limited:
# - EXECUTION_REPORT, ZERO_REPEATING_GROUP, REPEATING_GROUP, NESTED_REPEATING_GROUP have stale
#   BodyLength values (378/378/190/190 vs actual 387/353/153/200) but correct CheckSums; OtfParser
#   does not check BodyLength, so they are ported only as parse vectors.
# - ZERO_CHECKSUM_MESSAGE uses BodyLength "0067" (leading zeros); Artio's OtfParserTest only checks
#   the parse, so it is ported as parse + checksum, not validate.
# - GARBLED_MESSAGE ("4garbled9=") is defined but referenced by no test; skipped.
# - SessionParserTest / ExampleDictionary messages test session/dictionary semantics (CompID,
#   duplicate tags, enum values), not tag=value framing; skipped.
# - CommonDecoderImplTest covers decimal float decoding only; AsciiBufferTest covers integer/
#   MsgType decoding only; no FIX message vectors there.

